1️⃣ What is a Promise?

A Promise is an object that represents the result of an asynchronous operation.

It has 3 states:

pending → operation still running

fulfilled → operation succeeded

rejected → operation failed

2️⃣ Why do we need Promises?

Because asynchronous operations (setTimeout, API call, database, etc.) ka code callback hell create karta tha.

Promise solves:

nested callbacks ❌

messy flow ❌

hard debugging ❌

Promise gives:

clean code ✔

better flow ✔

easy error handling ✔

3️⃣ Promise Syntax
let promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    // async kaam
    if(success){
        resolve("Success value");
    } else {
        reject("Error happened");
    }
});

4️⃣ Promise Methods
✔ .then()

Runs when Promise is fulfilled.

promise.then(result => { ... })

✔ .catch()

Runs when Promise is rejected.

promise.catch(error => { ... })

✔ .finally()

Runs no matter success or failure.

promise.finally(() => { ... })

5️⃣ Promise Chaining

Ek promise ka result dusre promise ko pass karna.

doA()
  .then(doB)
  .then(doC)
  .then(result => console.log(result));

6️⃣ Example of Promise
function getData(){
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        setTimeout(() => {
            resolve("Data received");
        }, 1000);
    });
}

getData().then(res => console.log(res));

7️⃣ Promise vs Callback
Callback Hell ❌
step1(() => {
    step2(() => {
        step3(() => {
            step4();
        });
    });
});

Promise Flow ✔
step1()
  .then(step2)
  .then(step3)
  .then(step4);

8️⃣ Promise Utility Methods
✔ Promise.all()

Sab promises ko run karta hai.
Jab sab complete ho jaye → resolve.

Promise.all([p1, p2, p3])
  .then(result => console.log(result));

✔ Promise.race()

Jo promise sabse pehle complete hoga → uska result aayega.

✔ Promise.allSettled()

Saare results return karta hai (success/failure dono).

✔ Promise.any()

Jo pehla successfully resolve hoga → uska result.

9️⃣ Error Handling in Promises
fetchData()
  .then(res => JSON.parse(res))
  .catch(err => console.log("Error: ", err));

🔟 Converting Callback → Promise
function task(){
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    setTimeout(() => resolve("Done"), 1000);
  });
}

task().then(console.log);

1️⃣1️⃣ Async / Await (Promise ka modern version)
async function run(){
    let data = await getData();
    console.log(data);
}
run();

1️⃣2️⃣ Promise Flow Diagram (Simple)
New Promise
  |
  → pending
      |
      +→ resolve → fulfilled → then()
      |
      +→ reject  → rejected  → catch()

1️⃣3️⃣ IMPORTANT INTERVIEW POINTS

✔ Promise is eager (runs immediately)
✔ Promise is immutable once settled
✔ .then() always returns a new Promise
✔ async/await is built on top of Promises
✔ You must return Promise in chain